# Competency question: "What does each glossary interop lowering drop, per target?"
# The two shipped glossary lowerings (OntoLex vartrans, TBX/ISO-30042) are LOSSY
# sound-under-approximations: they carry the term↔term crossing faithfully but drop
# structure the canonical gmeow:Glossary holds. That loss is NOT hidden in generator
# prose — each lowering records a lang:ProjectionEmission carrying its
# lang:projectionTargetName, its non-Exact logic:preservationKind, and every dropped
# construct as a lang:unsupportedConstruct. This query reads that per-target loss ledger
# straight off the corpus: it selects every emission whose preservation kind is NOT
# logic:ExactPreservation and enumerates each construct it declares dropped.
#
# Worked instance: over the glossary-projection-loss fixture the answer is exactly the
# two glossary emissions' drops — the four OntoLex-vartrans drops and the six TBX drops —
# each row carrying its target name, its logic:SoundUnderApproximation judgment, and the
# one construct that target cannot carry. An Exact lowering (no drops) would not answer.
PREFIX lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?target ?preservation ?dropped WHERE {
    ?emission a lang:ProjectionEmission ;
        lang:projectionTargetName ?target ;
        logic:preservationKind ?preservation ;
        lang:unsupportedConstruct ?dropped .
    FILTER(?preservation != logic:ExactPreservation)
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?emission), "http://example.org/lang/"))
}
ORDER BY ?target ?dropped
